          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="case-wide" data-case-reveal><LiveDeckEmbed /></div>
      </section>
      <section id="case-chapter-1" class="case-section" data-case-chapter>
        <header class="case-section-heading" data-case-reveal>
          <span class="case-eyebrow"><span>02</span>Renderers</span>
          <h2
            id="describe-a-scene-once-then-let-the-engine-build-it"
            data-source-anchor="describe-a-scene-once-then-let-the-engine-build-it"
          >
            Defining scenes with reusable D3 renderers
          </h2>
        </header>
        <div class="case-reading case-copy" data-case-reveal>
          <p>
            Each scene describes its text, figure type, and rendering settings
            in a data object with a shared schema. A renderer registry connects
            that figure type to the appropriate D3 builder, which draws and
            animates the visual using the supplied data. Adding a new line-chart
            scene, for example, means supplying another set of content and
            settings to the existing line-chart builder.
          </p>
          <p>
            The explorer below uses the same builders as the full deck. Choose a figure, then open its scene definition to see how the data and display settings produce the result.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="case-wide" data-case-reveal><ChartExplorer /></div>
      </section>
      <section id="case-chapter-2" class="case-section" data-case-chapter>
        <header class="case-section-heading" data-case-reveal>
          <span class="case-eyebrow"><span>03</span>Consistency</span>
          <h2 id="under-the-hood" data-source-anchor="under-the-hood">
            Keeping the scenes consistent
          </h2>
        </header>
        <div class="case-reading case-copy" data-case-reveal>
          <p>
